(ned -- TOOLSETTER CENTER CALIBRATION, operator spec 2026-08-03)
(Setup: 3/8in rod in a toolholder, electrically continuous with the spindle,)
(positioned BY THE OPERATOR roughly over the puck centre, ~20 mm above it.)
(Step 1: probe down to find the puck top with this rod.)
(Step 2: from 0.75 in out in the 4 axis directions, drop 10 mm below the top)
(and probe inward; back off, then latch slowly. Each axis is centred by its)
(OWN opposing pair, so the rod radius cancels and the rod diameter never)
(enters the math.)
(Ends: puck RETRACTED first -- an energised solenoid leaks the air supply)
(down, learned 2026-08-02 the hard way -- and THEN the rod travels to the)
(centre it just detected, tip 5 mm above the surface. That is the zero)
(every later section starts from.)
(Results, CURRENT WORK FRAME: #3045 = centre X, #3046 = centre Y,)
(#3047 = puck top Z. Persisted -- the 30xx block lives in ned5_pb.var.)

o<cal_probe_center> sub

  #<f_probe>  = 200.0   (probe feed, operator 2026-08-03 doubled it)
  #<f_latch>  = 10.0    (latch feed, operator spec)
  #<f_trav>   = 500.0   (positioning moves)
  #<f_check>  = 400.0   (protective descent, kept at 2x the probe feed)
  (1 mm is plenty. If the probe does not release inside 1 mm the fault is)
  (electrical contact quality, not backoff distance -- do NOT paper over it)
  (by retreating further. Operator 2026-08-03.)
  #<backoff>  = 1.0
  #<r_out>    = 19.05   (0.75 in outward, operator 2026-08-03)
  #<under>    = 10.0    (probe depth below the detected top, operator spec)
  #<clear>    = 5.0     (hover height above the top between directions)

  o10 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL: switch to MM first - this routine is metric)
  o10 endif

  (pin the feed override: the operator saw 300 and 750 in the GUI because)
  (the F slider was at 150% - probes must run at their programmed feeds.)
  (on_abort restores M50 P1 if this cycle dies.)
  M50 P0

  G90
  #<sx> = #5420
  #<sy> = #5421

  (--- puck UP, timed dwell: there is no deployed sensor ------------------)
  M64 P3
  G4 P1.5

  (--- STEP 1: locate the top ---------------------------------------------)
  G91
  G38.2 Z-30 F[#<f_probe>]
  G1 Z[#<backoff>] F[#<f_trav>]
  G38.2 Z-[#<backoff> + 1] F[#<f_latch>]
  G90
  #<top> = #5063
  (BANK IT NOW. If anything later in this cycle aborts -- a missed edge, a)
  (probe left tripped -- the top is still a real measurement and must not be)
  (thrown away with the run. Operator 2026-08-03.)
  #3047 = #<top>
  (PRINT, CAL step 1: puck top at Z #<top> STORED to #3047, current work frame)
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]

  (--- STEP 2: 4 edges ------------------------------------------------------)
  (direction d: angle = d * 90 deg, so +X +Y -X -Y. dx = cos, dy = sin.)
  (Results in #100+d for X and #110+d for Y of each latched edge touch.)
  (Operator 2026-08-03: four axis-aligned touches instead of eight -- the)
  (diagonals cost time and add nothing, because each axis is already pinned)
  (by its own opposing pair.)
  #<d> = 0
  o100 while [#<d> LT 4]
    #<ang> = [#<d> * 90.0]
    #<dx> = COS[#<ang>]
    #<dy> = SIN[#<ang>]

    (out to 1 in from the operator centre, at hover height)
    G90 G1 X[#<sx> + #<r_out> * #<dx>] Y[#<sy> + #<r_out> * #<dy>] F[#<f_trav>]

    (protective descent to 10 mm under the top: if this TRIPS, the puck is)
    (still underneath us -- the operator centre is too far off, or the puck)
    (is bigger than 1 in radius. Never plunge blind.)
    G91
    G38.3 Z-[#<clear> + #<under>] F[#<f_check>]
    o110 if [#5070 EQ 1]
      M65 P3
      (abort, CAL: contact during descent at direction #<d> - recentre the rod and rerun)
    o110 endif

    (probe INWARD toward the operator centre: trips on the puck rim)
    G90
    G38.2 X#<sx> Y#<sy> F[#<f_probe>]

    (back off 1 mm outward, then latch in at 10 mm/min)
    G91
    G1 X[#<dx> * #<backoff>] Y[#<dy> * #<backoff>] F[#<f_trav>]
    G38.2 X[0 - #<dx> * [#<backoff> + 1]] Y[0 - #<dy> * [#<backoff> + 1]] F[#<f_latch>]

    #[100 + #<d>] = #5061
    #[110 + #<d>] = #5062

    (clear the rim, then hover)
    G1 X[#<dx> * 2 * #<backoff>] Y[#<dy> * 2 * #<backoff>] F[#<f_trav>]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]

    #<d> = [#<d> + 1]
  o100 endwhile

  (--- centre: each axis from its OWN opposing pair -------------------------)
  (+X touch is #100, -X touch is #102: their midpoint is the centre X, and)
  (the rod radius cancels in the pairing. Likewise +Y #111 against -Y #113.)
  #<cx> = [[#100 + #102] / 2]
  #<cy> = [[#111 + #113] / 2]

  #3045 = #<cx>
  #3046 = #<cy>

  (PRINT, CAL edges X: +X #100  -X #102     edges Y: +Y #111  -Y #113)
  (PRINT, CAL RESULT: centre X #<cx> Y #<cy> top Z #<top> STORED to 3045/3046/3047, work frame)
  (DEBUG, CAL done: centre X#<cx> Y#<cy>, top Z#<top>)

  (--- retract the puck FIRST, then travel to the detected zero -------------)
  (Operator 2026-08-03: the cycle must END sitting on the zero it just)
  (found, with the puck already down -- so the next section starts from the)
  (measured centre and nothing traverses over a raised puck.)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  M65 P3
  G4 P1.5
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<f_trav>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<clear>] F[#<f_trav>]
  M50 P1

o<cal_probe_center> endsub

M2 (end program)
